The Advanced Mode provides advanced options for experienced end-users to configure the  BIOS settings. The figure below shows an example of the  Advanced Mode. Refer to the  following sections for the detailed configurations.


notice:<PIC:Manual25_66>
{{image description: Small note-style icon showing a pen or feather on an otherwise blank white page; no readable technical text is visible.}}

To access the EZ Mode, click  EzMode (F7)  or press  <F7>.

<PIC:Manual25_67>
{{image description: ASUS UEFI BIOS Utility Advanced Mode screen with red callouts. It labels the menu bar, MyFavorite, Q-Fan control, EZ Tuning Wizard, Quick Note, Hot Keys, menu items, sub-menu item, general help, configuration fields, scroll bar, popup window, last modified settings, EZ Mode shortcut, and a hardware monitor sidebar.}}

##### Menu bar


The menu bar on top of the screen has the following main items:
<PIC:Manual25_68>
{{image description: Green table explaining BIOS menu bar tabs. My Favorites saves frequently used settings and configuration; Main changes basic system configuration; Ai Tweaker changes overclocking settings; Advanced changes advanced system settings; Monitor displays system temperature, power status, and fan settings; Boot changes system boot configuration; Tool configures special functions; Exit selects exit options and loads default settings.}}

The Advanced menu items allow you to change the settings for the CPU and other system  devices.<PIC:Manual25_82>
{{image description: ASUS UEFI BIOS Utility in Advanced Mode. The Advanced tab is selected and CPU Configuration is highlighted in a left menu that also includes Platform Misc Configuration, System Agent Configuration, PCH-IO Configuration, SATA Configuration, USB Configuration, Onboard Devices Configuration, APM Configuration, and Network Stack Configuration. A hardware monitor panel appears on the right.}}

Be cautious when changing the settings of the Advanced menu items. Incorrect field values can cause the system to malfunction.

- Select the source of the Windows 7 installation disk then click  Next.<PIC:Manual25_92>
{{image description: ASUS EZ Installer Step 1 of 3, Select your disc source. A dropdown shows an optical drive source and capacity 3181 MB, with Back and Next buttons.}}

- Select the USB storage device and click  next.<PIC:Manual25_93>
{{image description: ASUS EZ Installer Step 2 of 3, Insert a USB storage device. It asks for an 8 GB or larger USB storage device that will be formatted, shows a drive selection with capacity about 7519 MB, and has Back and Next buttons plus a refresh icon.}}

Click the refresh icon  if the USB storage device is not displayed.
- Click  Yes  to clear the contents on the USB storage device and create a  bootable USB device.
- Make sure to backup contents on the USB storage device, as it will be formatted.
- Once completed, click  OK  to finish.

- Windows 7 OS disk to ISO file<PIC:Manual25_94>
{{image description: ASUS EZ Installer window for creating a Windows 7 installation file to an ISO file. The dropdown reads Windows 7 OS disc to ISO file and a Next button is at the bottom right.}}

- Select  Windows 7 OS disk to ISO file  then click  Next.
- Check  I agree  and then click  Next.<PIC:Manual25_95>
{{image description: ASUS EZ Installer EULA screen for the ISO-file workflow, with license text, an I agree checkbox, Back button, and Next button.}}
